# Loge: egglog smoke test

```elixir
root = Path.expand("..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:loge, path: Path.join(root, "loge"), override: true},
  {:loge_egglog, path: Path.join(root, "loge_egglog")},
  {:kino_loge, path: Path.join(root, "kino_loge")}
])
```

## Running

Expected: **Success**, the extracted term `(Add (Num 2) (Num 3))` or `(Add (Num 3) (Num 2))`.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math) (Mul Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n(rewrite (Mul a (Num 1)) a)\n\n(let e (Add (Mul (Num 2) (Num 1)) (Num 3)))\n(run 5)\n(check (= e (Add (Num 3) (Num 2))))\n(extract e)\n",
  graph: false
)
```

With **Show the e-graph** on, the Result tab also draws the e-graph: each e-class a box of its e-nodes.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math) (Mul Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n(rewrite (Mul a (Num 1)) a)\n\n(let e (Add (Mul (Num 2) (Num 1)) (Num 3)))\n(run 5)\n",
  graph: true
)
```

A failed check: expected **No**, egglog's message in the Output tab.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math) (Mul Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n(rewrite (Mul a (Num 1)) a)\n\n(let e (Add (Mul (Num 2) (Num 1)) (Num 3)))\n(run 5)\n(check (= e (Num 5)))\n",
  graph: false
)
```

This run grows without bound. Expected: it runs until stopped; stopping the evaluation ends it.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJlbmdpbmUiOiJlZ2dsb2ciLCJsYW5ndWFnZSI6ImVnZ2xvZyIsIm9wdGlvbnMiOnsiZ3JhcGgiOmZhbHNlfSwic291cmNlIjoiKGRhdGF0eXBlIEUgKE51bSBpNjQpIChBZGQgRSBFKSlcbihydWxlICgoPSB4IChBZGQgYSBiKSkgKD0geSAoQWRkIGMgZCkpKSAoKEFkZCB4IHkpKSlcbihsZXQgZSAoQWRkIChOdW0gMSkgKE51bSAyKSkpXG4ocnVuIDEwKVxuIiwidmFyaWFibGUiOiIifQ","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype E (Num i64) (Add E E))\n(rule ((= x (Add a b)) (= y (Add c d))) ((Add x y)))\n(let e (Add (Num 1) (Num 2)))\n(run 10)\n",
  graph: false
)
```

## Includes

A **Logic Source** cell binds a datatype and its rules to `math`; a cell that includes
it with `(include "math")` runs them. Expected: **Success**, the extracted term
`(Add (Num 1) (Num 2))` or `(Add (Num 2) (Num 1))`.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJsYW5ndWFnZSI6ImVnZ2xvZyIsInNvdXJjZSI6IihkYXRhdHlwZSBNYXRoIChOdW0gaTY0KSAoQWRkIE1hdGggTWF0aCkpXG4ocmV3cml0ZSAoQWRkIGEgYikgKEFkZCBiIGEpKVxuIiwidmFyaWFibGUiOiJtYXRoIn0","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.SourceCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
math =
  Loge.source(
    :egglog,
    "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n"
  )
```

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJlbmdpbmUiOiJlZ2dsb2ciLCJpbnB1dCI6bnVsbCwibGFuZ3VhZ2UiOiJlZ2dsb2ciLCJvcHRpb25zIjp7ImdyYXBoIjpmYWxzZX0sInNvdXJjZSI6IihpbmNsdWRlIFwibWF0aFwiKVxuXG4obGV0IGUgKEFkZCAoTnVtIDEpIChOdW0gMikpKVxuKHJ1biAzKVxuKGNoZWNrICg9IGUgKEFkZCAoTnVtIDIpIChOdW0gMSkpKSlcbihleHRyYWN0IGUpXG4iLCJ2YXJpYWJsZSI6IiJ9","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(include \"math\")\n\n(let e (Add (Num 1) (Num 2)))\n(run 3)\n(check (= e (Add (Num 2) (Num 1))))\n(extract e)\n",
  graph: false,
  includes: %{"math" => math}
)
```

## Linting

Expected: under the editor, a parse error at the extra `)` on line 2.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJlbmdpbmUiOiJlZ2dsb2ciLCJsYW5ndWFnZSI6ImVnZ2xvZyIsIm9wdGlvbnMiOnsiZ3JhcGgiOmZhbHNlfSwic291cmNlIjoiKGRhdGF0eXBlIE0gKE51bSBpNjQpKVxuKGxldCB4IChOdW0gMSkpKVxuIiwidmFyaWFibGUiOiIifQ","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog, "(datatype M (Num i64))\n(let x (Num 1)))\n", graph: false)
